    "organism": "Arabidopsis thaliana",
    "taxonomy_id": "3702",
    "function_text": "Contributes to jasmonic acid biosynthesis by initiating the beta-oxidative chain shortening of its precursors (PubMed:16963437, PubMed:18267944). Converts 12-oxo-phytodienoic acid (OPDA) and 3-oxo-2-(2'-pentenyl)-cyclopentane-1-octanoic acid (OPC-8:0) into OPDA-CoA and OPC-8:0-CoA, respectively (PubMed:16963437, PubMed:18267944). Follows a two-step reaction mechanism, wherein the carboxylate substrate first undergoes adenylation by ATP, followed by a thioesterification in the presence of CoA to yield the final CoA thioester (By similarity)",
